Two patterns. The first is what you want for nearly everything.

**Pattern A — ccache, no credentials in task args**

```yaml
- name: IPA config
  hosts: ipaserver
  become: true
  gather_facts: false

  pre_tasks:
    - name: Check for automation keytab
      ansible.builtin.stat:
        path: "{{ svc_ansible_keytab }}"
      register: svc_ansible_kt
      tags: [always]

    - name: Obtain TGT
      ansible.builtin.command:
        cmd: kinit -kt {{ svc_ansible_keytab }} {{ svc_ansible_principal }}
      when: svc_ansible_kt.stat.exists
      changed_when: false
      tags: [always]

  tasks:
    - name: Ensure role groups present
      freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipagroup:
        name: "{{ item }}"
        description: "Service role group"
      loop: "{{ ipa_role_groups }}"

    - name: Ensure jump host HBAC rule
      freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipahbacrule:
        name: rdp-accounts-jumphosts
        hostgroup:
          - jumphosts
        usergroup:
          - rdp-accounts
        hbacsvc:
          - sshd
        state: present

    - name: Ensure sudo rule for platform admins
      freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipasudorule:
        name: platform-admin-all
        usergroup:
          - role-platform-admin
        hostgroup:
          - swarm-nodes
        cmdcategory: all
        state: present
```

No `ipaadmin_*` anywhere. The modules find root's ccache because `become: true`.

**Pattern B — explicit keytab per module**

Only when you can't rely on the ccache — a one-off play, or something running outside your normal entry point.

```yaml
- name: Ensure group present
  freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipagroup:
    ipaadmin_principal: "{{ svc_ansible_principal }}"
    ipaadmin_keytab: "{{ svc_ansible_keytab }}"
    name: role-artifactory-admin
```

Both parameters together — principal alone defaults to `admin` and the keytab lookup fails confusingly. The path resolves on the **node**, not the controller; that trips people who assume controller-side execution.

To avoid repeating it across many tasks, `module_defaults` keyed per module works:

```yaml
module_defaults:
  freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipagroup:
    ipaadmin_principal: "{{ svc_ansible_principal }}"
    ipaadmin_keytab: "{{ svc_ansible_keytab }}"
  freeipa.ansible_freeipa.ipahbacrule:
    ipaadmin_principal: "{{ svc_ansible_principal }}"
    ipaadmin_keytab: "{{ svc_ansible_keytab }}"
```

Verbose enough that Pattern A is usually the better answer.

**group_vars/ipaserver/main.yml**

```yaml
svc_ansible_principal: svc-ansible
svc_ansible_keytab: /etc/ipa/svc-ansible.keytab

ipa_role_groups:
  - role-artifactory-admin
  - role-artifactory-read
  - role-grafana-admin
  - role-grafana-read
```

**One behaviour worth knowing before you trust `--check`**

ansible-freeipa modules talk to the IPA API rather than managing local state, and check-mode support varies by module and version. Run `--check` against sbox first and confirm it reports what you expect — don't assume a clean dry run means a clean apply.